  "description": {
    "en": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (en): Zanthoxylum nitidum",
      "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zanthoxylum_nitidum",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 1340801690,
      "text": "Zanthoxylum nitidum, commonly known as shiny-leaf prickly-ash, is a species of flowering plant in the family Rutaceae. It is a woody climber with prickles on the branchlets, thick, cone-shaped spines on the trunk and older branches, pinnate leaves with five to nine leaflets, and panicles or racemes of white to pale yellow, male or female flowers in leaf axils and on the ends of branchlets."
    },
    "fr": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (fr): Zanthoxylum nitidum",
      "source_url": "https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zanthoxylum_nitidum",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 217124987,
      "text": "Zanthoxylum nitidum est une espèce de plantes à fleurs de la famille des Rutaceae. C'est un arbuste présent en Asie du Sud-Est et en Océanie. Il est surnommé \"shiny-leaf prickly-ash\" en anglais et liang mian zhen (两面针) en chinois."
    }
  },
